{"step_index":250,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T19:27:03Z","content":"I have completed the security and technical audit of the **StreamWave Entertainment** academic payment simulation and paid-library access control.\n\n---\n\n### 🛡️ Security & Technical Audit Findings\n\n| Audit Check | Status | Verification & Technical Safeguards Implemented |\n| :--- | :---: | :--- |\n| **1. Zero External Financial APIs** | **PASS** | `POST /api/demo-payment` executes 100% local Python simulation logic. No external payment gateway or network call (Stripe, EcoCash API, PayPal) is ever initiated. |\n| **2. Zero Sensitive Card / Mobile Transmission** | **PASS** | `DemoPaymentRequest` Pydantic model receives **ONLY** `email`, `method`, `plan_id`, and `simulate_decline`. Card numbers, CVVs, expiry dates, and mobile numbers remain in client DOM and are never posted to the backend. |\n| **3. No Financial Data in Logs / Cookies / URLs** | **PASS** | Structured JSON logs and session cookies contain strictly non-sensitive metadata: transaction reference, customer email, plan ID, timestamp, and status. |\n| **4. Strict Payment Method Whitelist** | **PASS** | `app.py` enforces `valid_methods = {\"ecocash\", \"visa\", \"mastercard\"}`. Any unauthorized string returns `HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity`. |\n| **5. Input Length & Schema Validation** | **PASS** | Pydantic fields enforce strict bounds: `email` (5–120 chars), `method` (3–20 chars), `plan_id` (max 50 chars), `media_id` (max 50 chars). |\n| **6. HMAC-SHA256 Signed HTTP-Only Cookie** | **PASS** | `streamwave_session` cookie is generated via HMAC-SHA256 signature using `DEMO_SESSION_SECRET` and set with `HttpOnly=True` and `SameSite=Lax`. |\n| **7. Vercel HTTPS Secure Cookie Mode** | **PASS** | Automatically detects Vercel HTTPS deployment (`os.getenv(\"VERCEL_ENV\") == \"production\"` or `os.getenv(\"VERCEL\") == \"1\"`) to enable `Secure=True`. |\n| **8. Cookie Tampering Rejection** | **PASS** | `verify_session_token()` performs constant-time HMAC signature verification (`hmac.compare_digest`). Any modified payload or signature returns `None`, rejecting access with `HTTP \n<truncated 159 bytes>\nto `/library` redirect to `/checkout`. |\n| **10. Protected API Access Control** | **PASS** | `/api/media`, `/api/media/{media_id}`, and `/api/play-events` are protected with `dependencies=[Depends(verify_paid_session)]`, returning `HTTP 401` when unpaid. |\n| **11. Anti-Duplicate Click Submissions** | **PASS** | Payment form buttons (`#submit-pay-btn` and `#decline-pay-btn`) are disabled immediately upon submission click during processing. |\n| **12. Sanitized Structured Logging** | **PASS** | `logger.info()` outputs JSON telemetry for `demo_payment_approved`, `demo_payment_declined`, and `playback_started` containing zero secrets or credentials. |\n| **13. Environment Secret Handling** | **PASS** | `DEMO_SESSION_SECRET` is dynamically read from `os.getenv(\"DEMO_SESSION_SECRET\")` and is never committed to source control. |\n| **14. Read-Only Serverless Filesystem** | **PASS** | Zero runtime filesystem writing occurs on Vercel. Event telemetry is streamed directly to stdout logs. |\n| **15. Member Media Playback** | **PASS** | Verified that 5-second MP4 movie previews (`/media/streamwave-preview.mp4`) and music audio samples (`/media/demo.wav`) remain fully functional on `/library` for paid members. |\n| **16. Automated Test Suite Verification** | **PASS** | Full automated unit test coverage across public endpoints, 401 rejections, payment simulations, cookie signatures, and media playback. |\n\n---\n\n### 📝 README Section Added\n\nThe [`README.md`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/README.md) has been updated with an explicit **Security & Payment Simulation Disclaimer** detailing:\n- Payment checkout is an academic simulation with zero financial gateway connections.\n- Demonstration membership cookies represent access simulation for coursework assessment.\n- Static media previews do not feature commercial DRM.\n- Production requirements (authorized payment gateway APIs, database persistence, private object storage with signed URLs, DRM encryption, and formal security review).","thinking":"**Summarizing the Audit**\n\nI'm now summarizing the audit findings! I'm reviewing the verification points to ensure a clear and concise report. Specifically, I've confirmed that no real payment provider or financial API is contacted. The system is 100% internal, which is a key point to emphasize in the report.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
