{"step_index":268,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T20:19:12Z","content":"The error occurred because Command Prompt was open in `C:\\Windows\\System32` instead of your StreamWave project folder.\n\nCopy and paste these commands into your Command Prompt window to navigate to the project folder and push to GitHub:\n\n### 1️⃣ Navigate to your project directory\n```cmd\ncd C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2️⃣ Run the Git Commands\n```cmd\ngit add .\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit commit -m \"feat: Add StreamWave landing page, simulated checkout, signed cookie access control, and logo watermark\"\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n*(Note: If your default branch is `master` instead of `main`, use `git push origin master`)*"}
