{"step_index":284,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T20:51:08Z","content":"I have created the [`vercel.json`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/vercel.json) configuration file so Vercel knows how to build and host your StreamWave FastAPI application!\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Push `vercel.json` to GitHub\n\nRun these 3 commands in your Command Prompt window:\n\n```cmd\ngit add .\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit commit -m \"chore: Add vercel.json for Vercel deployment\"\n```\n\n```cmd\ngit push origin main\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Deploy on Vercel (Easiest Method)\n\n1. Open **[vercel.com/new](https://vercel.com/new)** in your web browser.\n2. Log in with your **GitHub** account.\n3. Under **Import Git Repository**, look for **`unclechipaz/streamwave`** and click **Import**.\n4. Leave all default settings as they are and click **Deploy**! 🚀\n\nVercel will build your FastAPI application and give you a live production URL (e.g. `https://streamwave-xxxx.vercel.app`). \n\nEvery time you push new code to GitHub in the future, Vercel will automatically update your live site!"}
