{"step_index":296,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T21:01:25Z","thinking":"**Investigating Deployment Failure**\n\nI've confirmed the presence of `streamwave-logo.png` and `streamwave-preview.mp4` within the `public/` directory. My next step is to diagnose the root cause of the `FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED` error from Vercel. I'm focusing on scrutinizing `vercel.json` and the static files mounting configuration within FastAPI's `app.py`, particularly around line 509.\n\n\n**Analyzing Static Asset Handling**\n\nI'm now focusing on how FastAPI handles static routes when mounted at `/` in the Vercel `@vercel/python` environment. I'm considering whether static routes conflict with explicitly defined routes, given the order of mounting. I'm also confirming Vercel's builder uses `app` in `app.py`. Furthermore, I've checked the asset ensures. It's now clear that creating files in a directory mounted on the static path won't work on Vercel's serverless handler!\n\n\n**Diagnosing Filesystem Error**\n\n\\n\\n\n\nI've pinpointed the `FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED` error: it's a read-only filesystem issue. Calls to `mkdir()` and file checks at module level within `ensure_video_preview_asset()`, `ensure_logo_asset()`, and `ensure_favicon_assets()` attempt to modify `/var/task/public/media`, leading to an unhandled `OSError`.  I'm now implementing `try...except` blocks around these asset-handling functions to gracefully handle the read-only environment and prevent crashes.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import base64\\nimport hashlib\\nimport hmac\\nimport json\\nimport logging\\nimport os\\nimport shutil\\nimport time\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import List, Optional\\n\\nfrom fastapi import Depends, FastAPI, HTTPException, Path as PathParam, Query, Request, Response, status\\nfrom fastapi.responses import FileResponse\\nfrom fastapi.staticfiles import StaticFiles\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\\n\\n# Configure structured Python logger\\nlogging.basicConfig(\\n    level=logging.INFO, format=\\\"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(name)s: %(message)s\\\"\\n)\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\\\"streamwave\\\")\\n\\nBASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nDATA_FILE = BASE_DIR / \\\"data\\\" / \\\"media.json\\\"\\nPUBLIC_DIR = BASE_DIR / \\\"public\\\"\\nMEDIA_DIR = PUBLIC_DIR / \\\"media\\\"\\nIMAGES_DIR = PUBLIC_DIR / \\\"images\\\"\\n\\nPREVIEW_VIDEO_FILE = MEDIA_DIR / \\\"streamwave-preview.mp4\\\"\\nLOGO_IMAGE_FILE = IMAGES_DIR / \\\"streamwave-logo.png\\\"\\n\\n# Centralized Subscription Plan Configuration\\nSUBSCRIPTION_PLAN = {\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"streamwave-monthly\\\",\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"StreamWave Monthly\\\",\\n    \\\"price\\\": \\\"US$2.99 per month\\\",\\n    \\\"price_amount\\\": 2.99,\\n    \\\"currency\\\": \\\"USD\\\",\\n    \\\"interval\\\": \\\"month\\\",\\n    \\\"benefits\\\": [\\n        \\\"Full Zimbabwean catalogue access\\\",\\n        \\\"5-second MP4 movie previews\\\",\\n        \\\"Demonstration music audio samples\\\",\\n        \\\"Access on desktop or mobile\\\",\\n    ],\\n}\\n\\n# Session Cookie Signing Secret (Read from environment variable, never hardcoded in production)\\nDEMO_SESSION_SECRET = os.getenv(\\n    \\\"DEMO_SESSION_SECRET\\\", \\\"streamwave-secret-key-academic-demo-2026\\\"\\n).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef create_session_token(email: str, expiry_seconds: int = 86400 * 7) -> str:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Generates an HMAC-SHA256 signed session token for a paid demonstration member.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    payload = {\\n        \\\"email\\\": email.strip().lower(),\\n        \\\"plan_id\\\": SUBSCRIPTION_PLAN[\\\"id\\\"],\\n        \\\"exp\\\": int(time.time()) + expiry_seconds,\\n    }\\n    json_bytes \n<truncated 18762 bytes>","Description":"\"Wrap asset helper functions in safe try-except blocks to prevent crashes on Vercel read-only filesystem\"","