{"step_index":300,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T21:05:37Z","thinking":"**Investigating The Error**\n\nOkay, so I got a response from the serverless function! It's now working, but not quite as expected. I received JSON back, specifically `{\"detail\":\"Landing page not found\"}`. I need to understand why the `serve_landing_page()` function returned an HTTP 404 error with that message. This is the latest development in the thought process.\n\n\n**Analyzing Static File Handling**\n\nI've been examining why the landing page isn't being served correctly. It seems the issue stems from how Vercel handles static files in the `public/` directory versus my Python function. I've realized that Vercel's Edge CDN automatically serves these files, making my `FileResponse` unnecessary and actually conflicting with this automatic routing, which is why I'm receiving that 404 error. Now I need to see how to prevent `/` from routing to `app.py`.\n\n\n**Configuring Vercel Routing**\n\nI'm now focusing on standard Vercel configurations for FastAPI apps with static content. Specifically, I'm thinking I should route `/api/(.*)` to my `app.py` for API endpoints. Vercel's CDN would handle everything else in `public/`. This approach should allow Vercel to serve the static files and allow Python to only process specific routes. I'm imagining that I need to keep the static page routes in the Python app as a fallback for local Uvicorn dev.\n\n\n**Implementing Routing Strategy**\n\nI'm now in the thick of configuring the `vercel.json` file. The goal is to set up clean routing rules. I'm focusing on directing `/api/(.*)`, `/docs`, `/redoc`, and `/openapi.json` to my `app.py` backend. Static files and the default landing page routes will be handled directly from the `public/` directory by Vercel's CDN. I'm tracing the implications of this configuration step-by-step. It looks like `/` now serves `public/index.html` by default. This approach looks to be the official pattern.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"{\\n  \\\"version\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"builds\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"app.py\\\",\\n      \\\"use\\\": \\\"@vercel/python\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"routes\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/api/(.*)\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"app.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/docs\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"app.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/redoc\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"app.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/openapi.json\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"app.py\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/checkout\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"/checkout.html\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/library\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"/library.html\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"src\\\": \\\"/(.*)\\\",\\n      \\\"dest\\\": \\\"/$1\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"","Description":"\"Update vercel.json to route /api/* to FastAPI python function and serve static files directly via Vercel CDN\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\dell\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\\\\vercel.json\"","toolAction":"\"Updating vercel.json for Vercel CDN routing\"","toolSummary":"\"Updating vercel.json for Vercel CDN routing\""}}]}
